1
00:00:50,092 --> 00:00:51,969
How about a ride,
mister?

2
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,136
Jennifer.

3
00:00:55,639 --> 00:00:58,183
Oh, man, are you a sight
for sore eyes!

4
00:00:59,268 --> 00:01:00,727
Let me look at you.

5
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:03,814
Marty, you're acting
like you haven't
seen me in a week.

6
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,732
I haven't.

7
00:01:05,816 --> 00:01:08,527
Are you okay?
Is everything all right?

8
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:14,700
Oh, yeah.

9
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:17,536
Everything's great.

10
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:22,833
(EXPLOSIVE CRASHING)

11
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:24,585
(TIRES SCREECHING)

12
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:34,886
Marty!
You've got to come
back with me!

13
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:37,723
Where?

14
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:38,849
Back to the future.

15
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:45,105
Wait a minute.
What are you doing, Doc?

16
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:46,189
I need fuel.

17
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,861
Go ahead. Quick!
Get in the car.

18
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:54,448
No, no, no. Look, Doc,
I just got here, okay?

19
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:56,908
Jennifer's here.
We're gonna take
the new truck for a spin.

20
00:01:56,992 --> 00:02:00,078
Well, bring her along.
This concerns her, too.

21
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,955
Wait a minute, Doc.
What are you
talking about?

22
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:03,790
What happens to us
in the future?

23
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:06,460
What, do we become assholes
or something?

24
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:09,129
No, no, no.
You and Jennifer
both turn out fine.

25
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:10,255
It's your kids, Marty.

26
00:02:10,339 --> 00:02:12,424
Something has
got to be done
about your kids.

27
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:15,177
(TIRES SCREECHING)

28
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:22,809
Hey, Doc, we better back up.
We don't have enough
road to get up to 88.

29
00:02:22,893 --> 00:02:27,314
Roads? Where we're going,
we don't need roads.

30
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:29,775
Say, Marty!

31
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:32,944
Marty!
Marty, I wanted to show
you these new matchbooks

32
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:35,155
for my auto detailing
I had printed up.

33
00:02:39,034 --> 00:02:40,577
A flying DeLorean?

34
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,717
What the hell
is going on here?

35
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:26,808
(BOTH SCREAMING)

36
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:28,560
(HORN BLARING)

37
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:31,563
What the hell
was that?

38
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:32,689
Taxicab.

39
00:04:33,482 --> 00:04:35,442
What do you mean a "taxicab"?
I thought we were flying.

40
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:36,526
Precisely.

41
00:04:36,902 --> 00:04:38,945
All right, Doc.
What's going on, huh?

42
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:40,739
Where are we?
When are we?

43
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:44,409
We're descending
toward Hill Valley,
California,

44
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:49,623
at 4:29 p.m. on Wednesday,
October 21, 2015.

45
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,374
2015?

46
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,711
You mean
we're in the future.

47
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:55,921
Future.
Marty, what do you mean?

48
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,465
How can we be
in the future?

49
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:00,383
Jennifer...

50
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,179
I don't know how
to tell you this,

51
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:07,098
but you're
in a time machine.

52
00:05:07,182 --> 00:05:09,851
JENNIFER: And this is
the year 2015?

53
00:05:09,935 --> 00:05:11,853
October 21, 2015.

54
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:14,731
God, so, like,
you weren't kidding.

55
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:17,400
Marty, we can
actually see our future.

56
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:19,611
Doc, now, you said
we were married, right?

57
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:20,695
(HESITATING) Yeah...

58
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:23,031
Yeah?
Was it a big wedding?

59
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:25,033
Marty, we're gonna be able
to see our wedding.

60
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:27,077
Wow.
I'm gonna be able to
see my wedding dress.

61
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,161
Wow.

62
00:05:28,245 --> 00:05:29,246
God, I wonder
where we live.

63
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:31,957
I bet it's a big house
with lots of kids.

64
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,166
How many kids...
(DEVICE WHINING)

65
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,793
Doc! What the hell
are you doing?

66
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,044
Relax, Marty.

67
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:38,755
It's just a sleep-inducing
alpha rhythm generator.

68
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:39,840
She was asking
too many questions,

69
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:41,800
and no one should
know too much
about their future.

70
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,176
This way
when she wakes up,

71
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:45,095
she'll think it
was all a dream.

72
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,847
Then what did
you bring her for?

73
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:48,014
I had to do something.

74
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:51,601
She saw the time machine.
I couldn't just leave her
there with that information.

75
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:53,895
Don't worry. She's not
essential to my plan.

76
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,565
Well, you're the doc,
Doc.

77
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:57,774
Here's our exit.

78
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:29,264
First, you've
gotta get out
and change clothes.

79
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:31,558
Right now?
It's pouring rain.

80
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,521
Wait five more seconds.

81
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,989
Right on the tick.

82
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:49,451
Amazing.
Absolutely amazing.

83
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:53,288
Too bad the post office
isn't as efficient as
the weather service.

84
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:02,047
Excuse the disguise,
Marty,

85
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,090
but I was afraid you
wouldn't recognize me.

86
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:05,425
I went to
a rejuvenation clinic

87
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,010
and got
an all-natural overhaul.

88
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:10,972
They took out some wrinkles,
did a hair repair,
changed the blood,

89
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:13,975
added a good 30 or
40 years to my life.

90
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:17,437
They also replaced
my spleen and colon.
What do you think?

91
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:21,358
You look great, Doc.

92
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,362
The future.

93
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:28,490
Unbelievable.

94
00:07:28,573 --> 00:07:30,075
I gotta
check this out, Doc.

95
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,242
All in good time, Marty.

96
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:32,452
We're on a tight
schedule here.

97
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,955
Tell me about my future.
I mean, I know I make it big.

98
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:36,873
But what? Do I become,
like, a rich rock star?

99
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:39,125
Please, Marty, no one
should know too much
about their own destiny.

100
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,627
Right. Right.

101
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:41,753
I am rich, though, right?

102
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,589
Marty, please,
take off your shirt.

103
00:07:45,674 --> 00:07:48,259
Put on the jacket
and the shoes.

104
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:51,930
Got a mission
to accomplish.

105
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:07,821
Ah-ha.

106
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,280
Precisely on schedule.

107
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,413
Power laces.
All right.

108
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:36,099
(WATCH ALARM BEEPING)

109
00:08:36,975 --> 00:08:38,560
This thing doesn't fit.

110
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:40,603
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Size-adjusting fit.</i>

111
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,063
Pull out
your pants pockets.

112
00:08:42,147 --> 00:08:44,941
All kids in the future
wear their pants inside out.

113
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:46,443
Put on this cap.

114
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:49,195
Perfect.
You're the spitting image
of your future son.

115
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,321
What?

116
00:08:50,405 --> 00:08:52,407
Help me move
Jennifer over here.

117
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:54,117
So what's the deal?

118
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,577
Grab her feet.

119
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:58,288
All right.
Okay, now what?

120
00:08:58,997 --> 00:09:03,126
In exactly two minutes,
you go around the corner
into the Cafe '80s.

121
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:04,878
Cafe '80s?

122
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:07,589
It's one of those
nostalgia places,
but not done very well.

123
00:09:07,672 --> 00:09:10,300
Go in and order a Pepsi.
Here's a 50.

124
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:12,260
Then wait for
a guy named Griff.

125
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:14,137
Right. Griff.
Right.

126
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,182
Griff's going to
ask you about tonight.
Are you in or out?

127
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,725
Tell him you are out.

128
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:19,893
Whatever he says,
whatever happens,

129
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,227
say no,
you're not interested.

130
00:09:21,311 --> 00:09:22,353
Okay.

131
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:24,814
Then leave,
come back here
and wait for me.

132
00:09:25,982 --> 00:09:29,569
Don't talk to anyone,
don't touch anything,
don't do anything,

133
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:31,029
don't interact
with anyone

134
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:33,323
and try not to
look at anything.

135
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:34,783
I don't get it.
I thought you said

136
00:09:34,866 --> 00:09:36,117
this had something
to do with my kids.

137
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:38,328
Look what happens
to your son.

138
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,122
My son?

139
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,918
God, he looks
just like me.

140
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:48,755
"Within two hours
of his arrest,
Martin McFly Jr

141
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,090
"was tried,
convicted and sentenced

142
00:09:50,173 --> 00:09:52,842
"to 15 years in
a state penitentiary."

143
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:54,302
Within two hours?

144
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:55,887
The justice system works
swiftly in the future

145
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,139
now that they've
abolished all lawyers.

146
00:09:58,223 --> 00:09:59,641
Oh, this is heavy.

147
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,101
It gets worse.
Next week, your daughter

148
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,268
attempts to break him
out of jail,

149
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:04,604
and she gets sent up
for 20 years.

150
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,773
My daughter.
Wait a minute.
I have a daughter?

151
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,567
You see? This one event
starts a chain reaction

152
00:10:09,651 --> 00:10:11,444
that completely destroys
your entire family.

153
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:12,779
(EXCLAIMS)

154
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,949
Hey, Doc, this date...
This is tomorrow's newspaper.

155
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:18,118
Precisely, I already
went further ahead
into time

156
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:19,410
to see
what else happens.

157
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:20,995
I backtracked everything
to this one event.

158
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:22,122
That's why
we're here today,

159
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:23,665
to prevent this incident
from ever happening.

160
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:24,999
(BEEPING)

161
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:26,918
Damn! I'm late!

162
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,294
Wait a minute.
Where you going now?

163
00:10:28,378 --> 00:10:29,796
To intercept
the real Marty Jr.

164
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:32,298
You're taking his place.
Around the corner
at the Cafe '80s.

165
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:34,467
Guy named Griff.
Just say no!

166
00:10:35,093 --> 00:10:37,679
Hey, what about Jennifer?
We're not just gonna
leave her here.

167
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:38,847
Don't worry,
she'll be safe.

168
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:40,723
It'll just be
for a few minutes.

169
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:43,017
And, Marty,
be careful around
that Griff character.

170
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:46,563
He's got
a few short circuits
in his bionic implants.

171
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:51,526
MARTY: The future.

172
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,621
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Welcome to Texaco.</i>

173
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,875
<i>You can trust your car
to the system with the star.</i>

174
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:52,587
<i>Checking oil.
Checking landing gear.</i>

175
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,797
<i>(JAWS</i> THEME PLAYING)

176
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:00,762
(SCREAMING)

177
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,562
The shark
still looks fake.

178
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:11,940
(MUSIC BLARING)
<i>Hi, friends.
Goldie Wilson III</i>

179
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:13,816
<i>for Wilson Hover
Conversion Systems.</i>

180
00:12:14,192 --> 00:12:17,445
<i>You know, when my grandpa
was mayor of Hill Valley,</i>

181
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:19,906
<i>he had to worry
about traffic problems.</i>

182
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:22,742
<i>But now, you don't have
to worry about traffic.</i>

183
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:25,662
<i>I'll hover-convert
your old road car</i>

184
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:32,168
<i>into a skyway flyer
for only $39,999.95.</i>

185
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:35,588
<i>So come on down and see me,
Goldie Wilson III,</i>

186
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:38,841
<i>at any one of our 29
convenient locations.</i>

187
00:12:38,925 --> 00:12:41,010
<i>Remember,
keep 'em flying.</i>

188
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:47,642
('80S POP MUSIC PLAYING)

189
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,945
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

190
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:06,661
<i>It's got a hot salsa,
avocados,</i>

191
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:09,497
<i>cilantro mixed
with your choice
of beans,</i>

192
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,708
<i>chicken, beef or pork.</i>

193
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,252
Waiter. Waiter.

194
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,630
(WHIRRING)

195
00:13:17,714 --> 00:13:19,340
<i>Welcome to the Cafe '80s,</i>

196
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:23,136
<i>where it's always
morning in America,
even in the afternoon.</i>

197
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,721
(LAUGHING)

198
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:27,348
<i>Our special today is
mesquite-grilled sushi.</i>

199
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:29,767
<i>You must have
the hostage special!
Cajun style.</i>

200
00:13:29,851 --> 00:13:31,728
(DISTORTED)
<i>You must have
the hostage special!</i>

201
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:34,814
<i>You must have
the hostage special!</i>

202
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:38,067
Hey, hey, hey, guys!
Hey, hey, guys!

203
00:13:38,151 --> 00:13:39,736
All I want is a Pepsi.

204
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,826
Hey, McFly!

205
00:13:47,994 --> 00:13:50,246
Yeah.
I've seen you around.

206
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:53,249
You're Marty McFly's kid,
aren't you?

207
00:13:54,334 --> 00:13:55,543
Biff?

208
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,045
You're Marty Jr.

209
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:59,005
Tough break, kid.

210
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:02,050
Must be rough
being named after
a complete butthead.

211
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,509
What's that
supposed to mean?

212
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:05,178
Hello? Hello?
Anybody home?

213
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:06,554
Hey. Hey.

214
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:08,348
Think, McFly, think!

215
00:14:08,431 --> 00:14:11,267
Your old man?
Mr. Loser?

216
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:12,727
What?

217
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:13,811
That's right.

218
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,731
Loser with a capital "L."

219
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,817
Look, I happen to know
George McFly is
no longer a loser.

220
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:21,694
No, I'm not talking
about George McFly.

221
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:23,279
I'm talking
about his kid.

222
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:27,033
Your old man,
Marty McFly Sr.,

223
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,202
the man who
took his life

224
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,954
and flushed it
completely down the toilet.

225
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:34,540
I did?

226
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:37,794
(STUTTERING) I mean...
I mean, he did?

227
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:39,879
Hey, Gramps,

228
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:43,049
I told you two coats
of wax on my car,
not just one!

229
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:46,594
Hey, hey, I just put
the second coat on
last week.

230
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:48,388
Yeah?
With your eyes closed?

231
00:14:48,471 --> 00:14:49,555
Are you two related?

232
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:53,142
Hello? Hello?
Anybody home?

233
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:55,978
What do you think,
Griff just calls me
"Grandpa" for his health?

234
00:14:56,062 --> 00:14:57,980
He's Griff?
Gramps!

235
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,900
What the hell
am I paying you for?

236
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,986
Hey, kid, say hello
to your grandma for me.

237
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,446
Get out here, Gramps.

238
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:07,532
OLDEST BIFF:
Hey, take it easy!

239
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:12,036
And, McFly,
don't go anywhere!
You're next!

240
00:15:14,414 --> 00:15:16,666
BOY: This is a video game.

241
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,292
(MUSIC PLAYING ON VIDEO GAME)

242
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:20,086
I got it working.

243
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:22,505
My dad taught me
about these.

244
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:24,674
MARTY: It is <i>Wild Gunman.</i>

245
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,300
How do you play
this thing?

246
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,177
I'll show you, kid.

247
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:31,055
