What the hell
do you care?
We can afford it.

824
00:47:32,475 --> 00:47:34,185
The least we can do
with all that money

825
00:47:34,268 --> 00:47:36,312
is provide a better life
for our children.

826
00:47:36,395 --> 00:47:37,688
Hold on one second.

827
00:47:37,772 --> 00:47:40,858
Let's get this straight.
Marty is your kid,
not mine.

828
00:47:40,941 --> 00:47:42,068
And all the money
in the world

829
00:47:42,151 --> 00:47:43,986
wouldn't do jack shit
for that lazy bum.

830
00:47:44,070 --> 00:47:46,197
Stop it, Biff.
Just stop it.

831
00:47:46,280 --> 00:47:49,742
Look at him.
He's a butthead,
just like his old man was.

832
00:47:52,661 --> 00:47:56,290
Don't you dare speak
that way about George.

833
00:47:57,875 --> 00:48:00,211
You're not even
half the man he was.

834
00:48:00,878 --> 00:48:02,004
(GRUNTS)

835
00:48:02,088 --> 00:48:04,215
You son of a bitch!
Hey.

836
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:08,552
(GROANING)

837
00:48:08,886 --> 00:48:11,222
OLDER BIFF: Always
the little hothead, huh?

838
00:48:17,186 --> 00:48:19,313
You wanna
take a poke at me?

839
00:48:21,232 --> 00:48:22,650
(MAN LAUGHING)

840
00:48:22,733 --> 00:48:25,528
Damn it, Biff.
That's it. I'm leaving.

841
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:26,612
