borrowed some newspapers.

904
00:51:55,237 --> 00:51:56,697
I don't get it, Doc.

905
00:51:56,905 --> 00:51:58,866
I mean, how can all
this be happening?

906
00:51:58,949 --> 00:52:00,409
It's like we're in
hell or something.

907
00:52:00,492 --> 00:52:03,495
No, it's Hill Valley.
Although, I can't imagine
hell being much worse.

908
00:52:03,579 --> 00:52:05,247
(EINSTEIN WHIMPERING)

909
00:52:05,581 --> 00:52:08,292
Oh, Einie.
I'm sorry, boy.

910
00:52:09,043 --> 00:52:12,379
The lab is an awful,
awful, awful, awful mess.

911
00:52:13,672 --> 00:52:15,049
Attaboy.

912
00:52:15,758 --> 00:52:18,969
Obviously,
the time continuum
has been disrupted,

913
00:52:19,053 --> 00:52:21,472
creating this new
temporal event sequence

914
00:52:21,555 --> 00:52:23,307
resulting in this
alternate reality.

915
00:52:23,390 --> 00:52:24,433
English, Doc.

916
00:52:24,516 --> 00:52:26,810
Here, here, here.
Let me illustrate.

917
00:52:31,523 --> 00:52:35,653
Imagine that this line
represents time.

918
00:52:35,736 --> 00:52:40,532
Here's the present, 1985,
the future and the past.

919
00:52:42,284 --> 00:52:45,412
Prior to
this point in time,
somewhere in the past,

920
00:52:45,496 --> 00:52:47,956
the timeline skewed
into this tangent

921
00:52:48,040 --> 00:52:51,043
creating
an alternate 1985.

922
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:54,922
Alternate to you,
me and Einstein,

923
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:58,467
but reality for
everyone else.

924
00:53:02,763 --> 00:53:04,598
Recognize this?

925
00:53:04,848 --> 00:53:06,892
It's the bag
the sports book came in.

926
00:53:06,975 --> 00:53:09,853
I know,
because the receipt
was still inside.

927
00:53:09,937 --> 00:53:13,857
I found them in
the time machine
along with this.

928
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,532
It's the top
of Biff's cane.

929
00:53:21,615 --> 00:53:23,200
I mean,
Old Biff from the future.

930
00:53:23,283 --> 00:53:25,244
Correct. It was
in the time machine

931
00:53:25,327 --> 00:53:29,623
because Biff was
in the time machine
with the sports almanac.

932
00:53:30,290 --> 00:53:31,375
Holy shit.

933
00:53:31,458 --> 00:53:34,294
You see,
while we were
in the future,

934
00:53:34,378 --> 00:53:35,838
Biff got
the sports book,

935
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:38,257
stole the time machine,
went back in time,

936
00:53:38,340 --> 00:53:41,719
and gave the book to himself
at some point in the past.

937
00:53:42,010 --> 00:53:46,181
Look. It says right here

938
00:53:46,265 --> 00:53:48,434
that Biff made
his first million

939
00:53:48,517 --> 00:53:51,478
betting on a horse race
in 1958.

940
00:53:52,104 --> 00:53:53,397
He wasn't just lucky.

941
00:53:53,480 --> 00:53:56,984
He knew because he had
all the race results
in the sports almanac.

942
00:53:57,234 --> 00:53:59,945
That's how he made
his entire fortune.

943
00:54:00,654 --> 00:54:02,990
Look at his pocket
with a magnifying glass.

944
00:54:05,451 --> 00:54:06,994
The almanac.

945
00:54:07,828 --> 00:54:10,205
Son of a bitch
stole my idea.

946
00:54:11,039 --> 00:54:13,333
He must have been
listening when I...

947
00:54:15,294 --> 00:54:18,505
It's my fault.
The whole thing
is my fault.

948
00:54:18,589 --> 00:54:20,591
If I hadn't bought
that damn book,

949
00:54:20,674 --> 00:54:22,217
none of this would
have ever happened.

950
00:54:22,301 --> 00:54:23,427
Well, it's all
in the past.

951
00:54:23,510 --> 00:54:24,595
You mean the future?

952
00:54:24,678 --> 00:54:27,556
Whatever.
It demonstrates precisely

953
00:54:27,639 --> 00:54:29,433
how time travel
can be misused

954
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:32,644
and why the time machine
must be destroyed

955
00:54:32,728 --> 00:54:35,105
after we straighten
all of this out.

956
00:54:35,189 --> 00:54:37,274
Right. So we go
back to the future,

957
00:54:37,357 --> 00:54:39,485
and we stop Biff
from stealing
the time machine.

958
00:54:39,568 --> 00:54:42,112
We can't,
because if we travel

959
00:54:42,196 --> 00:54:44,656
into the future from
this point in time,

960
00:54:44,740 --> 00:54:48,285
it will be the future
of this reality,

961
00:54:49,077 --> 00:54:52,247
in which Biff is
corrupt and powerful

962
00:54:52,331 --> 00:54:54,249
and married
to your mother

963
00:54:54,333 --> 00:54:59,213
and in which this
has happened to me.

964
00:55:00,047 --> 00:55:01,173
(WHIMPERING)

965
00:55:04,718 --> 00:55:09,598
No. Our only chance
to repair the present
is in the past

966
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:13,811
at the point where
the timeline skewed
into this tangent.

967
00:55:13,894 --> 00:55:17,981
In order to put
the universe back
as we remember it

968
00:55:18,065 --> 00:55:20,400
and get back
to our reality,

969
00:55:20,484 --> 00:55:22,319
we have to find
out the exact date

970
00:55:22,402 --> 00:55:24,196
and the specific
circumstances

971
00:55:24,279 --> 00:55:27,115
of how, where
and when Young Biff

972
00:55:27,199 --> 00:55:29,618
got his hands on
that sports almanac.

973
00:55:32,412 --> 00:55:33,580
