Just get in the car,
butthead.

1209
01:07:42,350 --> 01:07:44,769
(STARTS ENGINE)
Who are you calling
butthead, butthead?

1210
01:07:45,478 --> 01:07:46,604
How do you know
how to do that?

1211
01:07:46,688 --> 01:07:49,148
Nobody can start
this car but me.

1212
01:07:49,232 --> 01:07:52,777
Just get in the car, Tannen.
Today's your lucky day.

1213
01:07:53,027 --> 01:07:54,445
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1214
01:07:55,363 --> 01:07:58,992
Hey! Hey!
Hey, watch where you're
driving, old man.

1215
01:07:59,534 --> 01:08:01,077
If you dent this car,
I'll kill you.

1216
01:08:03,454 --> 01:08:04,789
(EXCLAIMING)

1217
01:08:07,834 --> 01:08:09,627
This cost me
300 bucks!

1218
01:08:09,711 --> 01:08:11,754
Would you shut up
about the car?

1219
01:08:12,213 --> 01:08:14,132
Hey, and another thing.
How do you know
where I live?

1220
01:08:14,215 --> 01:08:16,426
Let's just say
we're related, Biff.

1221
01:08:16,509 --> 01:08:19,053
And that being the case,
I got a little present
for you.

1222
01:08:19,137 --> 01:08:21,264
Something that'll
make you rich.

1223
01:08:21,347 --> 01:08:22,348
You want to be rich,
don't you?

1224
01:08:22,432 --> 01:08:25,351
Oh, yeah. Sure. Right.
That's rich. (LAUGHS)

1225
01:08:25,435 --> 01:08:27,353
You're going
to make me rich?

1226
01:08:27,895 --> 01:08:31,107
You see this book?
This book tells
the future.

1227
01:08:31,190 --> 01:08:33,192
Tells the results of
every major sports event

1228
01:08:33,276 --> 01:08:34,485
till the end
of the century.

1229
01:08:34,569 --> 01:08:38,531
Football, baseball,
horse races, boxing.

1230
01:08:39,657 --> 01:08:43,453
The information in here
is worth millions,
and I'm giving it to you.

1231
01:08:43,536 --> 01:08:46,122
Well, that's very nice.
Thank you very much.

1232
01:08:46,205 --> 01:08:50,043
Now, why don't
you make like a tree
and get out of here?

1233
01:08:51,044 --> 01:08:54,797
It's leave, you idiot.
Make like a tree and leave.

1234
01:08:54,881 --> 01:08:57,091
You sound like a damn fool
when you say it wrong.

1235
01:08:57,175 --> 01:09:01,054
All right, then,
leave and take
your book with you.

1236
01:09:01,137 --> 01:09:04,807
Don't you get it?
You could make a fortune
with this book.

1237
01:09:04,891 --> 01:09:06,351
Let me show you.

1238
01:09:07,644 --> 01:09:09,062
(STATIC)

1239
01:09:10,647 --> 01:09:13,358
MAN ON RADIO:
<i>UCLA trails 17-16.</i>

1240
01:09:13,441 --> 01:09:16,778
<i>It's 4th and 11
with only 18 seconds
left of this game.</i>

1241
01:09:16,861 --> 01:09:19,989
<i>I'd say it's
all over for UCLA.</i>

1242
01:09:20,073 --> 01:09:23,826
Bet you a million bucks
UCLA wins it 19-17.

1243
01:09:23,910 --> 01:09:25,078
What are you,
deaf, old man?

1244
01:09:25,161 --> 01:09:27,497
He just said it was over.
You lost.

1245
01:09:27,580 --> 01:09:29,040
Oh, yeah?

1246
01:09:29,499 --> 01:09:30,833
(VOLUME INCREASING)
<i>Here comes Decker
with the kick.</i>

1247
01:09:30,917 --> 01:09:32,418
<i>It's up.
It looks good, folks!</i>

1248
01:09:32,502 --> 01:09:36,798
<i>It looks very good.
Field goal!
UCLA wins 19-17.</i>

1249
01:09:37,090 --> 01:09:41,010
<i>Listen to that
Coliseum crowd go wild.
Jim Decker...</i>

1250
01:09:41,094 --> 01:09:42,345
All right, pops.
What's the gag?

1251
01:09:42,428 --> 01:09:44,347
How did you know
what the score
was gonna be?

1252
01:09:44,430 --> 01:09:46,641
I told you.
It's in this book.

1253
01:09:46,724 --> 01:09:50,269
All you gotta do is
bet on the winner,
and you'll never lose.

1254
01:09:55,858 --> 01:09:58,444
All right.
I'll take a look at it.

1255
01:10:00,863 --> 01:10:02,949
OLDEST BIFF:
You damn fool!

1256
01:10:03,032 --> 01:10:05,952
Never, never leave
this book laying around.

1257
01:10:06,035 --> 01:10:08,955
Don't you have a safe?
No, you don't have a safe.

1258
01:10:10,123 --> 01:10:12,959
Get a safe.
Keep it locked up.

1259
01:10:13,042 --> 01:10:14,919
And until then,
keep it on you
like this.

1260
01:10:15,002 --> 01:10:16,045
Hey, what are you doing?

1261
01:10:16,129 --> 01:10:17,964
And don't tell
anybody about it,
either.

1262
01:10:18,047 --> 01:10:19,298
And there's
one more thing.

1263
01:10:19,382 --> 01:10:23,219
One day,
a kid or a crazy,
wild-eyed old man

1264
01:10:23,302 --> 01:10:24,846
who claims to
be a scientist

1265
01:10:24,929 --> 01:10:27,390
is going to come around
asking about this...

1266
01:10:27,473 --> 01:10:29,225
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

1267
01:10:30,017 --> 01:10:32,311
If that ever happens...

1268
01:10:49,203 --> 01:10:50,997
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1269
01:10:51,998 --> 01:10:54,292
I'm trapped. Doc.

1270
01:10:54,500 --> 01:10:55,668
<i>Doc, come in, Doc.</i>

1271
01:10:55,752 --> 01:10:57,587
Marty, what's the report?
<i>Biff's gone.</i>

1272
01:10:58,129 --> 01:10:59,255
He's got the book.

1273
01:10:59,338 --> 01:11:01,382
The old man's gone, too.
I'm locked in Biff's garage.

1274
01:11:01,466 --> 01:11:02,633
<i>You gotta fly
the DeLorean over here</i>

1275
01:11:02,717 --> 01:11:03,843
<i>and get me
the hell out of here.</i>

1276
01:11:04,177 --> 01:11:05,928
The address is
1809 Mason Street.

1277
01:11:06,012 --> 01:11:07,930
I can't take the DeLorean
out in the daylight,

1278
01:11:08,014 --> 01:11:09,932
but don't worry, Marty.
Somehow I'll get
over there.

1279
01:11:10,016 --> 01:11:13,352
Doc, wait a minute.
Doc. Hey, Doc. Doc.

1280
01:11:14,937 --> 01:11:16,355
Perfect.

1281
01:11:23,279 --> 01:11:26,073
I told you, Grandma.
I'm going to the dance.

1282
01:11:26,199 --> 01:11:28,159
WOMAN:
When you coming home?
The dance.

1283
01:11:28,242 --> 01:11:30,995
BIFF: I'll get home
when I get home.

1284
01:11:32,288 --> 01:11:35,208
Don't forget to turn
off the garage light.

1285
01:11:40,713 --> 01:11:41,923
(ENGINE STARTING)

1286
01:11:50,181 --> 01:11:51,599
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1287
01:11:52,683 --> 01:11:54,018
(BICYCLE BELL RINGING)

1288
01:12:07,156 --> 01:12:08,783
Marty. Marty!

1289
01:12:09,242 --> 01:12:10,660
Marty.

1290
01:12:12,662 --> 01:12:15,122
Marty, Marty. Damn!

1291
01:12:15,915 --> 01:12:18,000
Where is that kid?

1292
01:12:18,084 --> 01:12:19,794
(MUSIC PLAYING ON CAR STEREO)

1293
01:12:24,340 --> 01:12:26,425
Doc. Doc, come in.

1294
01:12:27,093 --> 01:12:28,636
<i>Come in, Doc.</i>

1295
01:12:29,387 --> 01:12:30,471
Marty! Marty, come in.

1296
01:12:30,763 --> 01:12:31,973
Doc.
(FEEDBACK)

1297
01:12:35,810 --> 01:12:37,103
Marty.

1298
01:12:38,145 --> 01:12:39,772
Oh, my...

1299
01:12:41,440 --> 01:12:43,442
Great Scott.

1300
01:12:59,041 --> 01:13:00,418
Oh, my God.

1301
01:13:05,631 --> 01:13:06,757
Doc, Doc, come in.

1302
01:13:06,841 --> 01:13:08,467
Marty,
what happened to you?

1303
01:13:08,551 --> 01:13:10,094
I went to Biff's house,
and you weren't there.

1304
01:13:10,177 --> 01:13:11,220
You must have
just missed me.

1305
01:13:11,304 --> 01:13:12,346
I'm in the back
of Biff's car.

1306
01:13:12,430 --> 01:13:14,473
He's on his way
to the Enchantment
Under the Sea dance.

1307
01:13:15,391 --> 01:13:17,393
Marty, listen,
we may have to abort
this entire plan.

1308
01:13:17,476 --> 01:13:18,895
It's getting
much too dangerous.

1309
01:13:18,978 --> 01:13:20,563
Don't worry.
The book is on
Biff's dashboard.

1310
01:13:20,646 --> 01:13:21,981
I'll grab it as soon
as we get to the school.

1311
01:13:22,064 --> 01:13:24,150
Marty, you must
be extremely careful

1312
01:13:24,233 --> 01:13:25,610
not to run into
your other self.

1313
01:13:25,693 --> 01:13:27,320
<i>My other self?</i>
Yes.

1314
01:13:28,029 --> 01:13:32,158
Remember, your mother is
at that exact same dance
with you. Yeah.

1315
01:13:32,241 --> 01:13:34,410
<i>Right. This could
get heavy, Doc.</i>

1316
01:13:34,493 --> 01:13:35,661
Heavy, heavy.

1317
01:13:35,745 --> 01:13:38,372
Marty, whatever happens,
you must not let
your other self see you!

1318
01:13:38,456 --> 01:13:40,666
The consequences
could be disastrous.

1319
01:13:40,750 --> 01:13:42,043
Excuse me, sir.

1320
01:13:42,126 --> 01:13:43,127
(GASPS)

1321
01:13:43,210 --> 01:13:44,754
Yes, you with the hat.

1322
01:13:44,837 --> 01:13:45,922
Who, me?

1323
01:13:46,005 --> 01:13:47,048
Yes.

1324
01:13:47,423 --> 01:13:51,177
Be a pal and hand me
a five-eighths inch wrench
out of that toolbox.

1325
01:13:52,261 --> 01:13:53,846
Five-eighths?

1326
01:13:55,514 --> 01:13:57,934
Don't you mean
three-quarters?

1327
01:13:58,684 --> 01:14:00,770
Why, you're right.

1328
01:14:01,562 --> 01:14:06,192
I presume you're
conducting some sort of
weather experiment.

1329
01:14:08,194 --> 01:14:11,280
That's right.
How did you know that?

1330
01:14:11,364 --> 01:14:15,326
I happen to have had
a little experience
in this area.

1331
01:14:15,409 --> 01:14:18,079
Yes, well, I'm hoping
to see some
lightning tonight.

1332
01:14:18,162 --> 01:14:21,207
Although, the weatherman
says there's not
gonna be any rain.

1333
01:14:21,290 --> 01:14:22,583
There's going to
be plenty of rain,
all right.

1334
01:14:22,667 --> 01:14:24,877
Wind, thunder,
lightning.

1335
01:14:24,961 --> 01:14:26,671
It's gonna be one
hell of a storm.

1336
01:14:26,754 --> 01:14:29,548
Well, thanks.
Nice talking to you.

1337
01:14:29,632 --> 01:14:33,469
Maybe we'll bump into
each other some time
again in the future.

1338
01:14:34,470 --> 01:14:36,097
Or in the past.

1339
01:14:46,899 --> 01:14:48,401
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1340
01:14:53,781 --> 01:14:55,574
(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

1341
01:15:17,179 --> 01:15:18,931
Doc, Doc! Come in!

1342
01:15:33,529 --> 01:15:34,947
(GIRLS EXCLAIMING)

1343
01:16:32,171 --> 01:16:34,965
BIFF: Where's that punk
Calvin Klein, anyway?

1344
01:16:35,049 --> 01:16:36,092
BOY: How am I
supposed to know, Biff?

1345
01:16:36,175 --> 01:16:37,259
I ain't his secretary.
(LAUGHING)

1346
01:16:37,343 --> 01:16:40,262
Well, go find him.
He caused 300 bucks
damage to my car,

1347
01:16:40,346 --> 01:16:42,890
and I owe him
a knuckle sandwich.
Get going!

1348
01:16:42,973 --> 01:16:44,266
Drink up, Biff.
Yeah, thanks.

1349
01:16:44,350 --> 01:16:45,351
Ain't you coming?

1350
01:16:45,434 --> 01:16:46,644
I'm reading.

1351
01:16:48,187 --> 01:16:49,730
(BOTTLE BREAKING)

1352
01:17:39,238 --> 01:17:41,448
Well, well, well,
Mr. Tannen.

1353
01:17:42,575 --> 01:17:44,326
How nice
to see you here.

1354
01:17:44,410 --> 01:17:47,496
Why, Mr. Strickland,
it's nice to see you, sir.

1355
01:17:47,580 --> 01:17:48,956
Is that liquor
I smell, Tannen?

1356
01:17:49,498 --> 01:17:51,000
(STUTTERING)
I wouldn't know.

1357
01:17:51,083 --> 01:17:52,334
I don't know what
liquor smells like,

1358
01:17:52,418 --> 01:17:53,627
'cause I'm too
young to drink it.

1359
01:17:53,711 --> 01:17:55,045
I see.

1360
01:17:55,504 --> 01:17:57,381
And what have we here?

1361
01:18:00,926 --> 01:18:04,430
Sports statistics,
interesting subject.
Homework, Tannen?

1362
01:18:04,513 --> 01:18:07,349
No, it ain't homework,
'cause I ain't at home.

1363
01:18:07,433 --> 01:18:08,809
(CHUCKLES)

1364
01:18:09,435 --> 01:18:10,561
You've got a real
attitude problem.

1365
01:18:10,644 --> 01:18:12,229
You know that, Tannen?
Just watch it.

1366
01:18:12,313 --> 01:18:13,355
Because one day,
I'll have you

1367
01:18:13,439 --> 01:18:15,900
right where I want you
in detention.

1368
01:18:15,983 --> 01:18:17,109
Slacker!

1369
01:18:29,955 --> 01:18:31,916
MARTY: Jesus,
you smoke, too?

1370
01:18:31,999 --> 01:18:34,752
LORRAINE: Marty, you're
beginning to sound
just like my mother.

1371
01:18:34,835 --> 01:18:36,253
Yeah, right.

1372
01:18:36,337 --> 01:18:39,632
When I have kids,
I'm going to let them
do anything they want.

1373
01:18:39,715 --> 01:18:41,217
Anything at all.

1374
01:18:41,300 --> 01:18:42,885
Yeah, I'd like to
have that in writing.

1375
01:18:42,968 --> 01:18:44,220
Yeah, me, too.

1376
01:18:44,303 --> 01:18:47,056
Marty,
why are you so nervous?

1377
01:19:42,361 --> 01:19:43,529
(DOOR CLOSES)

1378
01:20:52,264 --> 01:20:53,432
Yes!

1379
01:20:57,227 --> 01:20:58,312
No!

1380
01:21:01,106 --> 01:21:02,608
<i>"Oh Là Là?"</i>

1381
01:21:03,442 --> 01:21:04,943
<i>"Oh Là Là?"</i>

1382
01:21:07,112 --> 01:21:08,530
<i>"Oh Là Là?"</i>

1383
01:21:10,949 --> 01:21:12,201
(ANXIOUS GASPING)

1384
01:21:14,286 --> 01:21:15,621
Doc! Doc!

1385
01:21:15,704 --> 01:21:16,872
Hey, you.

1386
01:21:16,955 --> 01:21:18,540
Doc, come in!

1387
01:21:18,624 --> 01:21:19,875
DOC: <i>Marty, what's up?</i>

1388
01:21:19,958 --> 01:21:22,461
Doc! I'm in trouble.
I blew it.

1389
01:21:22,544 --> 01:21:23,670
Where's the book?

1390
01:21:23,754 --> 01:21:24,963
<i>Biff must still
have it with him.</i>

1391
01:21:25,130 --> 01:21:26,465
All I got is
the damn cover.

1392
01:21:26,548 --> 01:21:27,758
<i>And where's Biff?</i>

1393
01:21:27,841 --> 01:21:29,885
You're asking for it.
I don't know.

1394
01:21:29,968 --> 01:21:31,261
<i>Don't you have any
idea where he is?</i>

1395
01:21:31,345 --> 01:21:33,680
No! I mean, he could
be anywhere by now.

1396
01:21:33,764 --> 01:21:35,307
Marty, the entire
future depends on you

1397
01:21:35,391 --> 01:21:37,393
finding Biff and
getting that book back!

1398
01:21:37,476 --> 01:21:38,811
I know.
I just don't know where...

1399
01:21:38,894 --> 01:21:40,396
LORRAINE: Stop it!

1400
01:21:40,479 --> 01:21:43,982
Stop it, Biff.
You'll break his arm.
Stop it!

1401
01:21:48,070 --> 01:21:49,488
Of course!

1402
01:21:50,155 --> 01:21:52,199
I gotta go.
I got one chance!

1403
01:21:52,282 --> 01:21:54,326
My old man is
about to deck Biff!

1404
01:22:01,750 --> 01:22:02,960
Yes!

1405
01:22:16,265 --> 01:22:17,850
Talk about déjà vu.

1406
01:22:18,100 --> 01:22:19,726
Are you okay?

1407
01:22:39,538 --> 01:22:41,457
Okay, everybody,
let's back up now.

1408
01:22:41,540 --> 01:22:43,667
Let's back up.
Let's everybody
just back up

1409
01:22:43,750 --> 01:22:45,127
and give him
a little bit of room,
okay.

1410
01:22:45,210 --> 01:22:46,211
A little bit of air.

1411
01:22:46,295 --> 01:22:49,214
It's okay.
I know CPR. I know CPR.

1412
01:22:49,298 --> 01:22:50,424
Hey.

1413
01:22:50,507 --> 01:22:51,884
What's CPR?

1414
01:22:51,967 --> 01:22:53,051
You!

1415
01:22:56,889 --> 01:22:57,890
He's fine.

1416
01:22:57,973 --> 01:22:59,975
Hey, did you
just take his wallet?

1417
01:23:00,058 --> 01:23:01,768
He just took
that guy's wallet.

1418
01:23:02,227 --> 01:23:04,646
MARTY: <i>Doc, success.
I got it.</i>

1419
01:23:04,730 --> 01:23:06,648
Thank goodness.

1420
01:23:07,649 --> 01:23:09,318
Great, Marty.

1421
01:23:09,401 --> 01:23:11,320
As soon as I reload
the fusion generator,

1422
01:23:11,403 --> 01:23:13,780
I'll meet you on the roof
of the high school gym.

1423
01:23:13,864 --> 01:23:15,324
On the roof. 10-4.

1424
01:23:15,407 --> 01:23:16,992
Hey, it's him!

1425
01:23:17,075 --> 01:23:18,368
Hey, he's in disguise.

1426
01:23:18,452 --> 01:23:20,329
Guys, what's that?

1427
01:23:22,164 --> 01:23:23,874
Come on!
Let's get him!

1428
01:23:31,131 --> 01:23:32,257
Damn!

1429
01:23:41,725 --> 01:23:43,352
MARVIN: (SINGING)
<i>Earth angel</i>

1430
01:23:43,560 --> 01:23:46,313
<i>Please be mine</i>

1431
01:23:46,980 --> 01:23:49,107
<i>My darling dear</i>

1432
01:23:49,274 --> 01:23:52,486
<i>Love you for all time</i>

1433
01:23:53,111 --> 01:23:55,864
<i>I'm just a fool</i>

1434
01:23:57,699 --> 01:24:00,619
<i>A fool in love</i>

1435
01:24:02,120 --> 01:24:05,374
<i>with you</i>

1436
01:24:10,087 --> 01:24:11,380
(CROWD APPLAUDING)

1437
01:24:11,463 --> 01:24:13,507
All right!
Let's do another one.

1438
01:24:13,799 --> 01:24:16,093
Where did he go?
He just came in here!

1439
01:24:17,553 --> 01:24:18,720
MARTY: <i>Something
that really cooks.</i>

1440
01:24:18,804 --> 01:24:19,805
(CROWD CHEERING)

1441
01:24:19,888 --> 01:24:21,348
Look! How did he
get up on stage?

1442
01:24:21,431 --> 01:24:23,725
I don't know,
but when he gets down,
we're gonna nail him.

1443
01:24:23,809 --> 01:24:26,228
How the hell did
he change his
clothes so fast?

1444
01:24:26,311 --> 01:24:28,772
MARTY: <i>All right,
it's an oldie
