1594
01:38:05,963 --> 01:38:07,632
The doc's gone.

1595
01:38:30,488 --> 01:38:31,823
Mr. McFly!

1596
01:38:32,615 --> 01:38:33,658
Huh?

1597
01:38:36,494 --> 01:38:38,996
Is your name
Marty McFly?

1598
01:38:44,001 --> 01:38:45,503
Yeah.

1599
01:38:47,338 --> 01:38:49,590
I've got something for you.

1600
01:38:51,884 --> 01:38:53,511
A letter.

1601
01:38:54,595 --> 01:38:56,347
A letter for me?

1602
01:38:57,432 --> 01:38:59,058
That's impossible.

1603
01:39:00,685 --> 01:39:01,894
Who the hell are you?

1604
01:39:01,978 --> 01:39:03,104
Western Union.

1605
01:39:03,688 --> 01:39:06,107
Actually, a bunch of us
at the office
were kind of hoping

1606
01:39:06,190 --> 01:39:08,484
maybe you could
shed some light
on the subject.

1607
01:39:08,568 --> 01:39:13,030
See, we've had that
envelope in our possession
for the past 70 years.

1608
01:39:16,033 --> 01:39:18,953
It was given to us
with the explicit
instructions

1609
01:39:19,036 --> 01:39:23,207
that it be delivered
to a young man
with your description

1610
01:39:23,291 --> 01:39:27,086
answering to
the name of Marty
at this exact location

1611
01:39:27,920 --> 01:39:31,841
at this exact minute,
November 12, 1955.

1612
01:39:32,383 --> 01:39:33,718
We have a little bet
going as to whether

1613
01:39:33,801 --> 01:39:35,636
this Marty would
actually be here.

1614
01:39:35,720 --> 01:39:37,472
Looks like I lost.
(LAUGHING)

1615
01:39:38,389 --> 01:39:39,849
Did you say 70 years?

1616
01:39:39,932 --> 01:39:42,685
Yeah, 70 years,
2 months, 12 days
to be exact.

1617
01:39:42,768 --> 01:39:44,645
Here sign on line 6,
please.

1618
01:39:44,729 --> 01:39:46,105
Here you are.

1619
01:39:56,449 --> 01:39:58,784
It's from the doc!

1620
01:40:02,622 --> 01:40:05,500
"Dear Marty,
if my calculations
are correct,

1621
01:40:05,583 --> 01:40:07,168
"you will receive this
letter immediately after

1622
01:40:07,251 --> 01:40:10,171
"you saw the DeLorean
struck by lightning.

1623
01:40:10,254 --> 01:40:13,216
"First, let me assure you
that I'm alive and well.

1624
01:40:13,299 --> 01:40:16,761
"I've been living happily
these past eight months
in the year 1885.

1625
01:40:16,844 --> 01:40:19,764
"The lightning bolt..."
1885!

1626
01:40:20,431 --> 01:40:21,933
"September, 1885."

1627
01:40:22,767 --> 01:40:26,187
Wait, wait, kid!
Wait a minute.
What's this all about?

1628
01:40:26,270 --> 01:40:29,106
He's alive!
The doc's alive!

1629
01:40:29,857 --> 01:40:32,026
He's in the Old West,
but he's alive.

1630
01:40:32,109 --> 01:40:33,611
Yeah, but, kid,
you all right?

1631
01:40:34,111 --> 01:40:35,321
Do you need any help?

1632
01:40:35,947 --> 01:40:38,157
There's only one man
who can help me.

1633
01:40:38,241 --> 01:40:40,076
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

1634
01:40:44,121 --> 01:40:45,206
(SIGHS)

1635
01:40:47,583 --> 01:40:48,584
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1636
01:40:50,461 --> 01:40:52,505
(SCREAMING)

1637
01:41:35,506 --> 01:41:37,300
(EXCLAIMING)

1638
01:41:40,553 --> 01:41:42,013
